+# ADR 0004 — Single-attempt execution (O04 handoff draft)
+
+## Ownership and durable ordering
+
+Runtime.Executor is assembled by app from the SQLite store, workspace manager, and ZCode adapter factory. The execution package imports protocol-independent agent types; only internal/agent/zcode imports coder/acp-go-sdk v0.13.5. No production JSON-RPC transport was introduced.
+
+Run(ctx, runID) reads the existing immutable Run snapshot as an execution.Spec. It creates one Attempt/connection epoch, prepares one isolated workspace, and records one executions row. Migration 003 is additive. Stages are claimed → process_starting → process_started → session_ready → prompt_dispatching → prompt_finished → verifying → finished. prompt_dispatching must commit before calling the SDK Prompt method; a persistence error returns without submitting it. PID, workspace cwd, session ID, confirmed model/mode, and final outcome remain attached to that Attempt. No automatic retry or cross-restart PID adoption is implemented.
+
+The specification contains schemaVersion=1, snapshotId, prompt, an explicit profile, and optional validation commands. Profiles reference absolute bridge/backend/provider paths and model/mode; credentials are not embedded in the specification. Child environments copy only PATH/HOME/USER/LOGNAME/TMPDIR/LANG/LC_ALL plus deliberately constructed ZCode configuration. They do not inherit daemon credentials or unrelated cloud environment variables.
+
+## ACP adapter
+
+The bridge starts with serve --mode build. Initialize must negotiate protocol 1 and the O01 cancelRequest capability. NewSession must report build mode; explicit mode/model changes must read back consistently before Prompt. One connection is bound to one session. Notifications with another session ID fail execution. Filesystem/terminal callbacks are unadvertised and return unsupported. Production SDK logging is discarded; normalized notifications are persisted through the callback, and a storage error cancels execution rather than silently dropping output.
+
+Normalized agent events retain the typed SDK update payload. Final text is a bounded summary with an explicit truncation flag; complete individual events remain in the event log. A final end_turn starts the separate validation phase and is not itself a test-pass claim.
+
+Permissions/forms are first persisted as Interaction records and place the Attempt in waiting_input. With no supplied Answer callback they wait until cancellation/deadline, never auto-approve. With an explicit callback the decision commits first; adapter validation checks permitted option IDs or the O04 primitive boolean/string/enum form subset, and a separate callback records reply_attempted before returning the SDK response. Rich schemas, persistent API answer routing, idempotency keys, and exactly-once broker decisions remain O05. Answer callbacks must honor context cancellation.
+
+A cumulative active timer pauses during human waiting and resumes with its remaining budget. It is not reset by repeated questions. A separate wall deadline remains active. Expiry invalidates interactions and times out the owning Attempt. Already committed terminal state is preserved when recording uncertain teardown; it does not by itself prove that a process has exited.
+
+## Processes, verification, and results
+
+Each bridge and each validation command starts in its own process group. The current live handle owns its PID/group; recovery never signals an arbitrary database PID. Shutdown requests session/cancel when needed, closes input, waits for cooperative exit, then attempts SIGTERM and SIGKILL with bounded waits. It requires the group to disappear and the direct child to be reaped. If teardown or callback draining cannot be confirmed, the workspace stays durably held and the result reports ProcessStopped=false. Detached processes that deliberately leave the managed group require stronger supervision/containment; this is not an OS sandbox.
+
+The bridge is stopped before validation so the model cannot continue changing the checked tree. Validation uses executable + argv + a workspace-contained directory, timeout, and expected exit code. Captured diagnostic tails are bounded and known credential fields are redacted; byte/truncation metadata accompanies output. No validation steps yields validation=not_configured, never passed. A failing command yields a failed outcome.
+
+After process shutdown, the still-held workspace is scanned for file hashes and changes. Outcome/state/events and an execution:<attempt> workspace reference commit together, then the lease can be released. Persistence or cleanup failure retains ownership. O09 will provide export/download and remove the output reference only after its retention/export contract permits it. Result size limits can fail persistence; callers must not treat that as successful completion.
+
+## Current completion limits
+
+The managed session could not write the real sibling orchestrator directory, so this is a reviewed patch from a temporary copy. It also denied the forced process-group signal in TestProcessGroupStopsDescendant. Cooperative full-chain tests and storage/adapter checks passed, but O04 is not complete until the patch is applied and the forced-stop check passes on a normal local process-control environment. No real model was run, no CLI execution command was added, and no daemon was installed.
